{% from "partials/enterprise/macros.njk" import arrow, ph %}
{% from "partials/enterprise/icons.njk" import icon %}
{%- set faqs = [
  ["Why is web application security testing important?", "Web application security testing helps businesses identify weaknesses before attackers exploit them. It helps protect customer information, reduce security risks, strengthen access controls and improve the reliability of web-based applications."],
  ["What vulnerabilities can web application security testing identify?", "Security testing can identify SQL injection, cross-site scripting (XSS), broken access controls, authentication weaknesses, insecure file uploads, security misconfigurations and sensitive data exposure. Testing can also reveal weaknesses in application logic, APIs and third-party components."],
  ["What is the difference between vulnerability assessment and web application penetration testing?", "A vulnerability assessment identifies and classifies potential security weaknesses across an application. Web application penetration testing goes further by safely validating selected vulnerabilities through controlled attack simulations to understand their potential impact."],
  ["How does CipherTrivia conduct web application security testing?", "CipherTrivia combines automated security tools with manual testing techniques to assess application vulnerabilities. Our process includes scope definition, security assessment, vulnerability validation, risk prioritization and reporting with practical remediation recommendations."],
  ["Which types of web applications can be tested?", "Our web app security testing services cover e-commerce websites, SaaS platforms, enterprise applications, customer portals, financial applications, healthcare platforms and web-based APIs. The testing scope is defined according to the application's functionality and security requirements."],
  ["How long does web application security testing take?", "The duration depends on application complexity, the number of features and user roles, the testing scope and the depth of manual assessment required. A focused assessment may take a few days, while larger applications can require several weeks."],
  ["What do you receive after web application security testing?", "CipherTrivia provides a web application security testing report containing identified vulnerabilities, severity ratings, supporting evidence, potential impacts and remediation recommendations. Retesting results may also be provided when verification is included in the agreed scope."],
  ["Can web application security testing help with compliance requirements?", "Security testing can support compliance initiatives by identifying application-level weaknesses and documenting security findings. The assessment can be aligned with relevant security standards or organizational requirements, although testing alone does not guarantee compliance or certification."],
  ["How often should web application security testing be performed?", "Testing is recommended before major application releases and after significant changes to application functionality, authentication or infrastructure. Periodic assessments can also help identify new vulnerabilities as applications, dependencies and threat conditions evolve."],
  ["Does CipherTrivia provide remediation support after testing?", "CipherTrivia provides practical remediation guidance to help development teams understand and address identified vulnerabilities. Additional remediation assistance and retesting can be discussed based on your application requirements and the agreed project scope."],
  ["How can I choose the right web app security testing company?", "Look for a web app security testing company that combines automated scanning with manual validation, provides clear risk ratings and delivers actionable remediation guidance. Review the provider's testing methodology, reporting quality, scope definition and approach to handling sensitive application data before selecting a partner."]
] %}

