<section class="section section--paper" id="types" aria-labelledby="s2-title">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="shead">
      <div class="shead__meta"></div>
      <div class="shead__body">
        <h2 class="shead__title rv" id="s2-title">Types of Web App Security Testing Services We Provide</h2>
        <p class="shead__lede rv" style="--d:1">CipherTrivia offers web app security testing services to identify vulnerabilities and assess security risks across websites and web applications. Our testing approach combines automated tools with manual assessment techniques to uncover weaknesses, validate potential attack paths and provide actionable recommendations that help businesses protect sensitive data and strengthen application security.</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="ledger">
      <article class="ledger__cell rv">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("radar") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Web Application Vulnerability Assessment</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">We examine web applications to identify security weaknesses, outdated components, insecure configurations and potential entry points for attackers. This assessment helps businesses understand their security gaps and prioritize vulnerabilities based on severity and potential impact.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:1">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("target") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Web Application Penetration Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Our web application penetration testing evaluates how attackers could exploit identified vulnerabilities through controlled attack simulations. We test authentication, access controls, session management and application functionality to identify exploitable weaknesses before they lead to security incidents.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:2">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("identity") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Authentication &amp; Access Control Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">We assess login mechanisms, password policies, session handling and user permissions to identify weaknesses that could allow unauthorized access. Testing also checks for broken access controls that may expose restricted pages, customer records or administrative functions.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:3">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("api") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">API Security Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">We evaluate APIs connected to web applications to identify weaknesses in authentication, authorization, data validation and access restrictions. Our API security testing helps detect vulnerabilities that could expose sensitive information or allow unauthorized actions through application endpoints.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("syringe") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Input Validation &amp; Injection Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">We test how applications handle user-supplied data to identify vulnerabilities such as SQL injection, cross-site scripting (XSS) and other injection-related risks. The assessment helps determine if improper input handling could expose databases, compromise application functionality or affect users.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:1">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("flowchart") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Business Logic Security Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">We review application workflows and business rules to identify weaknesses that automated scanners may overlook. Testing can uncover issues involving unauthorized transactions, workflow manipulation, pricing logic and misuse of application features.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:2">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("sliders") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Security Configuration &amp; Component Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">We assess security-related configurations, HTTP headers, exposed services and outdated software components that may increase application risk. This helps identify misconfigurations and known vulnerabilities that could weaken the application's overall security posture.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:3">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("retest") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Web Application Retesting</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">After vulnerabilities have been fixed, we can retest the affected areas, where included in the agreed scope, to verify remediation. This helps development teams confirm whether security issues have been resolved and identify any remaining weaknesses.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

